Validation required before upstream submission
---------------------------------------------
1. Run `go test ./pkg/common/health/...` with the mock-clock tests.
2. Add/confirm a test that, after recovery, the next scheduled check returns to
   `readyCheckInterval` rather than remaining on the recovery cadence.
3. Add/confirm a sustained-failure test proving repeated unhealthy checks use
   `readyCheckRecoveryInterval` and do not spin.
4. Benchmark or instrument representative server health checks to confirm that
   the shorter cadence during failure does not create unacceptable dependency
   load.
5. Decide with maintainers whether 5 seconds is the right constant or should be
   configurable.
6. Preserve the existing one-minute healthy steady-state cadence unless the
   maintainers intentionally broaden the scope of #7236.

Non-goals
---------
- This draft does not make `/ready` or `/live` execute checks synchronously.
- It does not eliminate the up-to-one-minute delay before a new failure is first
  detected in healthy steady state.
- It specifically reduces stale-unhealthy recovery time after a failure has been
  observed.
- It does not claim that a 5-second interval is an accepted SPIRE API/default.
